Good catch! Looking at the documentation:

> **before_agent_start** - Fired after user submits prompt, before agent loop. Can inject a message and/or append to the system prompt.

So `before_agent_start` fires **every time the user sends a prompt** (before each agent response), not just at session start.

This means the extension:
1. **`session_start`** - Shows the notification once at the beginning
2. **`before_agent_start`** - Appends to the system prompt **before every single user prompt**, repeatedly telling the agent to invoke the skill

This is potentially redundant - the agent would be reminded to invoke the skill on every turn, even if it already did. The author may have intended this as a persistent nudge, but it could also be unintentional duplication.

If the intent was to only remind once at session start, the `systemPromptAppend` logic should probably be in `session_start` or use some state tracking like:

```typescript
let reminded = false;

pi.on("before_agent_start", async (event, ctx) => {
  if (reminded) return;
  const harnessDir = findHarnessDir(ctx.cwd);
  if (harnessDir) {
    reminded = true;
    return { systemPromptAppend: "..." };
  }
});
```

